Abstract = {The occurrence of complete decapitation as a consequence of car accident
   is an extremely rare event. This fatality is generally seen in
   pedestrians run over by trains and also in motorcyclists who impact
   against the tailboard of trucks. Moreover, complete transection of
   pedestrians and occupants of cars has been described in road accidents
   especially in case of vehicles traveling at a high speed. We present a
   case of decapitation with complete degloving injury of the neck in a
   patient involved in a traffic accident, and we briefly discuss the
   possible mechanisms producing this injury.},
